analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment at end of remove method:

```java
public boolean remove(Object o) {
    int i = indexOf(o);
    if (i == -1)
        return false;
    else {
        removeAt(i);
        return true;
    }
    // @@@ If the element was in the queue before removal, the method returns true.
}
``We need to express: if the element was in the queue before removal, method returns true. Need to use \old to refer to pre-state. The condition "element was in the queue before removal" can be expressed as this.contains(o) before, or indexOf(o) != -1. Use observer methods: contains(Object) is public. So we can write: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true . Or equivalently: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result. Since result is boolean, \result == true is same as \result. So assert: assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result;.

Check syntax: need parentheses maybe: assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result;.

Make sure only public observer methods: contains is public. Use \old. Good.

